      "message": "Give a person's page its tabs, and count what they judged\n\nA person's page is five pages now, under one head: what stands, what\nlanded, the agents in their name, what they judged, and the allowance\nonly they and the operator see. Each tab is its own handler and its\nown queries, so nothing is computed for a tab nobody opened, and no\nrepository may take a tab's name under an owner.\n\nStanding draws the record the way it is read: four figures on shared\nrows, every claim by what happened to it, and thirteen weeks of\nlandings as bars. Weeks, not days: a landing needs the policy, so a\nweek cannot be painted by a script. Landed is the diary, newest first,\neach row saying whether a runner re-ran the revision that landed and\nlinking its signed receipt, with where the landings went and where in\nthe tree they touched beside it. Agents shows the split of landings\nbetween the person and the agents they hold, which ownership records\nand nobody types, and each agent with its own record and holds.\nJudgement counts what the person decided on other people's changes:\nlooks given, approvals, blocks and whether a block held, attempts\ncompared, questions answered, and the looks the attention budget asked\nof them. The rail says what is happening now, the organisations they\nare on, what they hold, and how to reach them. An agent's page is the\nsame in agent clothing, and somebody with nothing witnessed yet sees\nthe shape of the record and one sentence, not zeros as headlines. Every\nlist holds only what the viewer may read.\n\nChange-Id: Itabs0163\nTask: t-1rns7yg3z9attcyhq76rv34exp\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
